{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"withoutActuallyEscaping","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"ClosureType","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ResultType","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Failure","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"_","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"closure","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s23withoutActuallyEscaping_2doq_x_q_xq0_YKXEtq0_YKs5ErrorR0_r1_lF11ClosureTypeL_xmfp","text":"ClosureType","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"do","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"body","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": (","kind":"text"},{"text":"_","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"internalParam","text":"escapingClosure"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"ClosureType","preciseIdentifier":"s:s23withoutActuallyEscaping_2doq_x_q_xq0_YKXEtq0_YKs5ErrorR0_r1_lF11ClosureTypeL_xmfp"},{"text":") ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"Failure","preciseIdentifier":"s:s23withoutActuallyEscaping_2doq_x_q_xq0_YKXEtq0_YKs5ErrorR0_r1_lF7FailureL_q0_mfp","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ResultType","preciseIdentifier":"s:s23withoutActuallyEscaping_2doq_x_q_xq0_YKXEtq0_YKs5ErrorR0_r1_lF10ResultTypeL_q_mfp","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s23withoutActuallyEscaping_2doq_x_q_xq0_YKXEtq0_YKs5ErrorR0_r1_lF7FailureL_q0_mfp","text":"Failure","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s23withoutActuallyEscaping_2doq_x_q_xq0_YKXEtq0_YKs5ErrorR0_r1_lF10ResultTypeL_q_mfp","text":"ResultType","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Failure","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Error","text":"Error","preciseIdentifier":"s:s5ErrorP","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"kind":"parameters","parameters":[{"name":"closure","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A nonescaping closure value that is made escapable for the"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"duration of the execution of the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"body"},{"type":"text","text":" closure. If "},{"code":"body","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" has a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"return value, that value is also used as the return value for the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withoutActuallyEscaping(_:do:)"},{"text":" function.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"body","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A closure that is executed immediately with an escapable copy of","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"closure"},{"type":"text","text":" as its argument."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Return Value","anchor":"return-value"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The return value, if any, of the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"body"},{"text":" closure.","type":"text"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","text":"Discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You can use this function to call an API that takes an escaping closure in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a way that doesn’t allow the closure to escape in practice. The examples"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"below demonstrate how to use "},{"code":"withoutActuallyEscaping(_:do:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"conjunction with two common APIs that use escaping closures: lazy"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"collection views and asynchronous operations."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The following code declares an "},{"code":"allValues(in:match:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" function that checks"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whether all the elements in an array match a predicate. The function won’t"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"compile as written, because a lazy collection’s "},{"code":"filter(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" method"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"requires an escaping closure. The lazy collection isn’t persisted, so the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"predicate","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" closure won’t actually escape the body of the function;"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"nevertheless, it can’t be used in this way."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["func allValues(in array: [Int], match predicate: (Int) -> Bool) -> Bool {","    return array.lazy.filter { !predicate($0) }.isEmpty","}","\/\/ error: closure use of non-escaping parameter 'predicate'..."],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"withoutActuallyEscaping(_:do:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" provides a temporarily escapable copy of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"predicate","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" that "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"can","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" be used in a call to the lazy view’s "},{"code":"filter(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"method. The second version of "},{"code":"allValues(in:match:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" compiles without"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"error, with the compiler guaranteeing that the "},{"code":"escapablePredicate","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"closure doesn’t last beyond the call to "},{"code":"withoutActuallyEscaping(_:do:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["func allValues(in array: [Int], match predicate: (Int) -> Bool) -> Bool {","    return withoutActuallyEscaping(predicate) { escapablePredicate in","        array.lazy.filter { !escapablePredicate($0) }.isEmpty","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Asynchronous calls are another type of API that typically escape their"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"closure arguments. The following code declares a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"perform(_:simultaneouslyWith:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" function that uses a dispatch queue to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"execute two closures concurrently."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["func perform(_ f: () -> Void, simultaneouslyWith g: () -> Void) {","    let queue = DispatchQueue(label: \"perform\", attributes: .concurrent)","    queue.async(execute: f)","    queue.async(execute: g)","    queue.sync(flags: .barrier) {}","}","\/\/ error: passing non-escaping parameter 'f'...","\/\/ error: passing non-escaping parameter 'g'..."],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"code":"perform(_:simultaneouslyWith:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" function ends with a call to the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"sync(flags:execute:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" method using the "},{"code":".barrier","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" flag, which forces the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"function to wait until both closures have completed running before"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"returning. Even though the barrier guarantees that neither closure will"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"escape the function, the "},{"code":"async(execute:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" method still requires that the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"closures passed be marked as "},{"code":"@escaping","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so the first version of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"function does not compile. To resolve these errors, you can use"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"withoutActuallyEscaping(_:do:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" to get copies of "},{"code":"f","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"g","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" that can be"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"passed to "},{"code":"async(execute:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["func perform(_ f: () -> Void, simultaneouslyWith g: () -> Void) {","    withoutActuallyEscaping(f) { escapableF in","        withoutActuallyEscaping(g) { escapableG in","            let queue = DispatchQueue(label: \"perform\", attributes: .concurrent)","            queue.async(execute: escapableF)","            queue.async(execute: escapableG)","            queue.sync(flags: .barrier) {}","        }","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"name":"Important","type":"aside","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The escapable copy of ","type":"text"},{"code":"closure","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" passed to ","type":"text"},{"code":"body","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is only valid","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"during the call to ","type":"text"},{"code":"withoutActuallyEscaping(_:do:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". It is undefined","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"behavior for the escapable closure to be stored, referenced, or executed","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"after the function returns.","type":"text"}]}],"style":"important"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"sections":[],"metadata":{"title":"withoutActuallyEscaping(_:do:)","externalID":"s:s23withoutActuallyEscaping_2doq_x_q_xq0_YKXEtq0_YKs5ErrorR0_r1_lF","symbolKind":"func","platforms":[{"deprecated":false,"unavailable":false,"introducedAt":"8.0","beta":false,"name":"iOS"},{"deprecated":false,"unavailable":false,"introducedAt":"8.0","beta":false,"name":"iPadOS"},{"deprecated":false,"unavailable":false,"introducedAt":"13.0","beta":false,"name":"Mac Catalyst"},{"deprecated":false,"unavailable":false,"introducedAt":"10.10","beta":false,"name":"macOS"},{"deprecated":false,"unavailable":false,"introducedAt":"9.0","beta":false,"name":"tvOS"},{"deprecated":false,"unavailable":false,"introducedAt":"1.0","beta":false,"name":"visionOS"},{"deprecated":false,"unavailable":false,"introducedAt":"2.0","beta":false,"name":"watchOS"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"withoutActuallyEscaping"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"ClosureType"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"ResultType"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Failure"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s23withoutActuallyEscaping_2doq_x_q_xq0_YKXEtq0_YKs5ErrorR0_r1_lF11ClosureTypeL_xmfp","text":"ClosureType"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"do"},{"kind":"text","text":": ("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"_"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"internalParam","text":"escapingClosure"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s23withoutActuallyEscaping_2doq_x_q_xq0_YKXEtq0_YKs5ErrorR0_r1_lF11ClosureTy